e generation, §FS-test-contract.4.5).\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:370:### 3.5 Drive narrow `typeReached` conditions\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:373:conditions, preferably `typeReached` (§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.1). A\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:379:  \"condition\": { \"typeReached\": \"io.netty.util.Recycler\" },\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:412:stack trace and cover it per §FS-test-contract.1.5.\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:478:instrumentation, or native-image substitution paths (§FS-test-contract.4.5).\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:487:the failure anyway is the §FS-test-contract.4.2 violation, not a workaround\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:505:normally, so the helper is never a skip (§FS-test-contract.4.1).\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:559:representable behavior (§FS-test-contract.3.2).\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:572:explicit-timeout floor (§FS-test-contract.1.7) exists because\ndocs/functional-spec/test-contract.md:574:a warm JVM, and the 60-second bound (§FS-test-contract.1.6) still applies to\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:12:Image is normative in the test contract (§FS-test-contract), which makes\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:28:  §FS-test-contract.1 (what a test must have),\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:29:  §FS-test-contract.2 (what it must not do), §FS-test-contract.4 (the Native\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:32:  §FS-test-contract.3 (what a test should do). In review they are advisory: a\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:149:1. **Scaffold-only test** (§FS-test-contract.1.3). The review bar is exact:\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:157:2. **Native Image dodging** (§FS-test-contract.4.1, §FS-test-contract.4.2).\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:161:   loading (§FS-test-contract.4.3), are the same violation.\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:162:3. **Fake requested-metadata coverage** (§FS-test-contract.2.4). Metadata a\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:169:   (§FS-test-contract.1.5).\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:170:4. **Coverage bought by asserting breakage** (§FS-test-contract.2.6). A\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:173:5. **Version-pinned test** (§FS-test-contract.2.5) — unless the version check\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:175:6. **Visibility bypass** (§FS-test-contract.2.2). The test lives in the\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:178:7. **Compiling against fiction** (§FS-test-contract.2.3). Source stubs, fake\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:181:8. **Fix by weakening** (§FS-test-contract.2.9). A compile or runtime repair\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:186:9. **Condition cheating.** A metadata entry's `typeReached` condition names a\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:190:   (§FS-test-contract.3.5); an *invalid* condition is this must violation.\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:234:the reviewer commits it (§FS-test-contract.2.9). The review states what it\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:239:Native Image cannot support (§FS-test-contract.4.5) when the refusal cannot be\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:240:verified. Where none of the three proofs of §FS-test-contract.4.3.1 can be\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:244:The sanctioned repair is the re-scope of §FS-test-contract.4.3.2: drop that\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:302:(§FS-test-contract.4.5): the library guards that access itself, the guard fails\ndocs/functional-spec/contribution-contract.md:368:§FS-test-contract.4.3.2.\ndocs/functional-spec/README.md:18:| [§FS-test-contract](test-contract.md#fs-test-contract-the-test-contract) | The test contract |\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:55:- **Conditional on `typeReached`, and nothing else.** Every reachability-metadata\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:56:  entry is gated on a `condition` whose only key is `typeReached`.\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:57:  `typeReached` is the sole condition key the vendored schema accepts; no other\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:83:separation: any entry whose `type` or `condition.typeReached` names a test\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:93:Native tracing can observe an entry whose `condition.typeReached` belongs to a\ndocs/functional-spec/metadata.md:98:dependency closure and locates `typeReached` in the runtime-visible view of\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md:7:§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2 and, point by point, in §FS-test-contract;\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md:25:  necessity rule of §FS-test-contract.2.7.\ndocs/functional-spec/tests.md:33:§FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2 and §FS-test-contract; the rules below are a\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:31:Two properties make this achievable: the reachability-metadata schema is itself additive (every entry is gated on `typeReached`), and `native-image` defaults to runtime initialization when no build-time directives are supplied. The hard constraints below preserve that additivity — they are not editorial scope choices but direct consequences of the invariant.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:57:- Validation that every metadata entry uses `typeReached` and stays inside `allowed-packages`.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:187:**3. `<groupId>/<artifactId>/<metadata-version>/reachability-metadata.json`** — the only file the plugin loads at native-image time. Schema [reachability-metadata-schema-v1.2.0.json](../../metadata/schemas/reachability-metadata-schema-v1.2.0.json) (a vendored copy of the upstream GraalVM schema), with top-level keys `reflection`, `jni`, `resources`, `bundles`, `serialization`, and `foreignCalls`. Every entry's `condition` carries exactly one key, `typeReached`, so the plugin can rely on conditional registration; `typeReached` is the schema's only condition form. The legacy split-config layout (`reflect-config.json`, `jni-config.json`, …) is no longer present.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:224:- **Conditional registration.** Every metadata entry must use [Conditional Configuration](https://www.graalvm.org/latest/reference-manual/native-image/metadata/#specifying-reflection-metadata-in-json): a `condition` whose only key is `typeReached`, so registration is gated on actual reachability. `typeReached` is the sole condition form the vendored schema accepts; the older `typeReachable` is not valid and is rejected by `checkMetadataFiles`.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:225:- **Allowed-package conditions.** Every metadata entry's `typeReached` condition must reference a class inside the artifact's `allowed-packages`.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:229:- **Dependency and test-only split.** Metadata can declare dependencies on other artifacts via `requires`. Metadata needed only by the tests — entries whose type or `typeReached` names a test package, or whose resource is a test resource — must not ship to consumers; `splitTestOnlyMetadata` moves them out of the library's `reachability-metadata.json` into the test project's `src/test/resources/META-INF/native-image/reachability-metadata.json`, keeping the shipped metadata free of test-only types (§FS-metadata).\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:234:- **Test contract.** Every test must satisfy the test contract (§FS-test-contract): the normative statement of what a test must have, must not do, should do, and how it behaves under Native Image.\ndocs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md:280:- **Image-size discipline.** Conditional configuration (`typeReached`) is mandatory so consumers do not pay for metadata they do not exercise.\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1790542115732}]}
